WEBVTT

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:08.500
Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.580
ima wa ugokenai sore ga sadame dakedo

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.580
Right now I can't move... That is my fate, but...

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:20.720
akirame wa shinai mou mezameta kara

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:20.720
I won't give up anymore because I have awakened.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:25.890
moeru tokimeki wa jidai wo utsushi

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:25.890
My burning, throbbing heart reflects the era...

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.060
iro azayaka ni moesakaru honoo

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.060
It has the color of vividly blazing flames...

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.820
Crying ima wa mienaku tomo

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.820
Crying, though I can't see it right now...

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.350
Searching michi shirube wa ukabu

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.350
Searching, a guidepost floats up ahead.

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:43.170
I wanna have a pure time!

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:48.280
Everyone's a noble mind!

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:53.500
soko ni nokotta wakasa toridashi

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:53.500
I'll take out what remains of my youth there,

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:55.980
Believing a sign of Zeta,

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.540
beyond the hard times from now!

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:06.320
kawaku kuchibiru nureteiru nara

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:06.320
If these dry lips become wet,

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:11.460
toki wo norikoe atsui jidai e to

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:11.460
Beyond time, towards a passionate era,

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.500
utsuru darou to shinjiteiru kara

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.500
Because I believe it will move...

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:19.060
Believing a sign of Zeta,

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:23.690
beyond the hard times from now...

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:35.100
Inside the Capsule

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:38.130
Luna II.

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:41.800
It is a planetoid brought in
from the asteroid belt...

00:01:41.870 --> 00:01:45.430
...to mine its contents
for use at the colonies.

00:01:46.310 --> 00:01:49.280
Because of its proximity to Green Oasis
it's being used as a base...

00:01:49.350 --> 00:01:52.510
...for the Earth Federation Forces.

00:02:11.740 --> 00:02:13.600
What are you having trouble understanding?

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:17.070
The Minovsky particles
have increased in density.

00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:19.270
It's obvious that the troops chasing us...

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:22.510
...have challenged Gryps
to a mobile suit battle.

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:24.180
Lila Milla Rira!

00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:26.220
Could you please watch your language?

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:28.880
Then give me a chance to
get out my frustration.

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:30.720
You'll have your chance.

00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:33.550
The troops coming after us are
unmistakably from the A.E.U.G..

00:02:33.990 --> 00:02:35.320
I certainly hope so.

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:47.340
Commander Bright here! I'm coming in!

00:02:49.370 --> 00:02:52.570
I appreciate you coming
all the way here to Gryps.

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:53.800
It's my duty, sir.

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:57.140
This is a hand-written letter.

00:02:57.220 --> 00:03:00.240
Deliver this to Admiral Jamitov Hymem.

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:01.310
Yes, sir.

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:04.850
What's wrong?

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:05.890
Nothing, sir.

00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:07.920
Give it to him in person.

00:03:07.990 --> 00:03:09.590
Yes, sir. Excuse me.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:13.730
What time's the ship leaving?

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:15.200
In one hour.

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:16.730
Have a safe journey!

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:18.700
Thank you, sir.

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:20.870
- What is it?
- Sir!

00:03:21.670 --> 00:03:25.940
The troops on Luna II appear to have
detected the ship that...

00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:27.770
...may be responsible for dispatching
the mobile suits.

00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:32.250
You're certain that Lieutenant Franklin's
son stole the Gundam Mk. II?

00:03:44.230 --> 00:03:48.130
I've come across the Newtype Amuro Ray's
name in the underground press many times.

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:50.960
Really. Underground material
on Green Oasis?

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:54.800
Green Oasis wasn't initially a military base.

00:03:55.810 --> 00:03:59.300
That's true, but what were you going to do
if the air kept leaking?

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:02.880
We were able to obtain two mobile suits
with your help.

00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:04.750
It normally would be impossible to do.

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:07.910
It's nothing but coincidence.

00:04:09.250 --> 00:04:14.750
I prefer to believe that coincidences
result from the abilities of the person.

00:04:15.890 --> 00:04:17.380
Lieutenant Quattro here.

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:18.690
Yes, I'm on my way.

00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:20.860
- Are they coming?
- Probably.

00:04:20.930 --> 00:04:21.660
Great!

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:25.570
Ensign Reccoa! Take care of Kamille!

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:27.230
Yes, Commodore Blex!

00:04:27.310 --> 00:04:28.430
Enemies?

00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:33.040
I'd say. Since we're the only ones
deployed in this area...

00:04:33.110 --> 00:04:35.310
...it's safe to assume everyone
else is an enemy.

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:38.780
Lila, I trust you understand. Stop them
and conduct an official inspection.

00:04:38.850 --> 00:04:40.780
Our objective is not to destroy them.

00:04:40.950 --> 00:04:41.920
<i>I know.</i>

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:44.910
<i>Do I look like I enjoy war that much?</i>

00:04:44.990 --> 00:04:45.680
Yes, you do.

00:04:46.490 --> 00:04:48.550
<i>Then I'll have to prove myself</i>
<i>some other time.</i>

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:58.870
Am I hoping for too much?

00:04:58.940 --> 00:05:00.910
I'd like to think that he's a Newtype.

00:05:01.670 --> 00:05:03.400
What do you think, Lieutenant Quattro?

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:05.440
Newtypes aren't psychic.

00:05:06.140 --> 00:05:09.440
Therefore, I find nothing
different about him visually...

00:05:09.510 --> 00:05:11.240
...but I sense some qualities in him.

00:05:11.320 --> 00:05:13.280
I agree. Take good care of him.

00:05:13.350 --> 00:05:14.410
Yes, sir.

00:05:19.290 --> 00:05:20.820
Find anything, Astonaige?

00:05:21.230 --> 00:05:24.250
They're building a battleship
in the Gryps dock.

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:25.460
What kind of battleship?

00:05:25.530 --> 00:05:28.620
I can't tell. But it looks pretty big.

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:31.730
Make sure you make a few copies
of the Gryps data.

00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:33.670
There's a good chance
we're heading for battle.

00:05:33.740 --> 00:05:35.430
Huh?! Have we been discovered?

00:05:35.670 --> 00:05:39.800
Luna II's troops have had us under
surveillance ever since we arrived.

00:05:40.210 --> 00:05:41.270
Good point.

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:43.500
Kamille!

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:46.010
Yes, Lieutenant Quattro?

00:05:47.250 --> 00:05:50.920
Are you aware that a battleship
is being constructed at Gryps?

00:05:51.190 --> 00:05:52.520
At Green Noa 2?

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:55.360
Yes, I know.
But I don't know the details.

00:05:55.590 --> 00:05:56.720
I guess you wouldn't.

00:05:56.930 --> 00:06:00.560
Data indicates that the armor on the Gundam
Mk. II is the same as previous models.

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:01.430
But is that true?

00:06:01.700 --> 00:06:04.360
Yes, my mother mentioned it.

00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:06.130
- Your mother?
- Yes.

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:08.140
My mother specializes in
material engineering.

00:06:08.210 --> 00:06:08.970
Really.

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:13.310
She also said they will be using
different armor for the next mobile suit...

00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:14.570
...after the Gundam Mk. II.

00:06:14.650 --> 00:06:17.110
It sounds like the Mk. II will never
be upgraded.

00:06:17.320 --> 00:06:20.510
My father says he plans
to incorporate Zeon's technology...

00:06:20.590 --> 00:06:22.550
...into the line after the Mk. II.

00:06:25.590 --> 00:06:27.320
<i>Residential Modules lockdown, complete!</i>

00:06:27.390 --> 00:06:29.880
<i>Retract the bridge!</i>

00:06:49.350 --> 00:06:51.780
Can't we get a view of the A.E.U.G. yet?!

00:06:52.620 --> 00:06:55.520
We're told the Mont Blanc has confirmed
a pursuing vessel!

00:06:55.590 --> 00:06:57.320
What'll we do, Captain?!

00:06:57.520 --> 00:07:00.080
I don't like the course we're on right now.

00:07:00.630 --> 00:07:03.060
They may find us this way, but we'll
doubleback to Green Oasis...

00:07:03.130 --> 00:07:04.650
...and head for Earth!

00:07:04.730 --> 00:07:05.460
Yes, sir!

00:07:07.300 --> 00:07:08.290
What's wrong, Captain?

00:07:09.100 --> 00:07:11.360
Yes, we'll end up returning
to Green Oasis.

00:07:11.640 --> 00:07:12.760
Is that so?

00:07:12.840 --> 00:07:13.830
Let me see.

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:14.630
Sir.

00:07:14.710 --> 00:07:19.010
If we come from Green Oasis and avoid
Luna II, that will be our new route.

00:07:19.310 --> 00:07:23.010
This way we're less likely to be caught
by the garrison around Green Oasis.

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:25.810
Right. There will be some risk
no matter what route we take.

00:07:36.830 --> 00:07:40.160
If we're only observing the enemy mobile
suits, why does my wife have to join us?

00:07:40.370 --> 00:07:43.560
There's always the chance we'll get
our hands on the enemy's armor.

00:07:43.870 --> 00:07:46.360
Are you suggesting we do
a material quality check in a battlefield?!

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:48.030
These are Captain Bask's orders.

00:07:48.670 --> 00:07:51.840
Captain. Lieutenants Franklin
and Hilda have boarded!

00:07:52.410 --> 00:07:55.850
Okay, prepare the Alexandria for take off!
Open gate!

00:07:56.380 --> 00:07:58.610
So these two are Kamille's parents.

00:07:58.680 --> 00:08:00.670
Just watch, Blex.

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:19.800
You seem to know what to do.

00:08:20.170 --> 00:08:21.800
Send a signal flare to the Bosnia.

00:08:25.740 --> 00:08:27.440
- They've found us!
- What?!

00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:33.010
I found you! Damn A.E.U.G. thieves!

00:08:34.790 --> 00:08:37.050
I'm amazed, it's only the two ships!

00:08:39.690 --> 00:08:41.590
What's that ship?!

00:08:41.790 --> 00:08:43.760
That's not a Federation Forces battleship!

00:08:43.930 --> 00:08:46.400
Did the A.E.U.G. build that themselves?

00:08:47.200 --> 00:08:48.530
What's going on?

00:08:49.100 --> 00:08:52.070
We're supposed to inspect it,
but will they let us?

00:08:52.570 --> 00:08:54.230
Mobile suits, prepare for take off!

00:08:54.770 --> 00:08:56.470
<i>Stand by to fire!</i>

00:08:57.940 --> 00:08:59.100
A halt signal?!

00:09:01.050 --> 00:09:02.380
Are they telling us to stop?

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:07.080
I don't think they believe
we're dispatching our own forces.

00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:09.210
That's because they aren't
Titans from Gryps!

00:09:09.990 --> 00:09:11.320
They're Galbaldies!

00:09:11.390 --> 00:09:13.120
- Four units!
- That many?

00:09:13.490 --> 00:09:15.930
Lieutenant Quattro,
standby with your Rick Dias...

00:09:15.990 --> 00:09:17.760
...so that you can take off at any time.

00:09:19.900 --> 00:09:20.960
Maintain speed!

00:09:31.140 --> 00:09:32.440
It's fast.

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:36.810
They're not slowing down.
Very suspicious!

00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:44.720
Don't assume a battleship
can beat a mobile suit.

00:09:49.760 --> 00:09:50.730
It's here!

00:09:51.300 --> 00:09:52.520
Hold your fire!

00:09:55.870 --> 00:09:56.990
A Galbaldy!

00:09:57.440 --> 00:09:59.960
It's a Galbaldy from the Bosnia
at Luna II!

00:10:00.640 --> 00:10:02.200
We could be leaving!

00:10:02.910 --> 00:10:05.430
<i>Wait a little longer!</i>
<i>I don't want to open fire first.</i>

00:10:05.680 --> 00:10:08.340
Can you hear me?!
Identify your vessel's affiliation!

00:10:08.410 --> 00:10:12.110
<i>If you continue to ignore my orders,</i>
<i>I will have no choice but to fire!</i>

00:10:14.650 --> 00:10:17.050
We are the A.E.U.G.
Your orders are meaningless!

00:10:17.320 --> 00:10:20.020
- Roger, then I will open fire.
- I don't think so!

00:10:22.390 --> 00:10:23.880
- What the...!
- Nice move!

00:10:26.330 --> 00:10:27.300
There!

00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:30.520
What?

00:10:32.770 --> 00:10:34.400
Mobile suits, launch!

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:46.680
Is it true that Kamille stole
a Gundam Mk. II?

00:10:46.750 --> 00:10:48.480
How should I know?

00:10:49.020 --> 00:10:51.110
You're always like that.

00:10:51.860 --> 00:10:53.650
Only thinking about yourself.

00:10:56.190 --> 00:10:58.590
Right now, I'm thinking about Bask.

00:10:58.660 --> 00:11:01.430
I know very well that these circumstances
are very odd.

00:11:01.500 --> 00:11:06.060
Are you sure you're not thinking about
that young lady, Margarita?

00:11:09.640 --> 00:11:12.270
This is a normal suit for pilots, right?

00:11:12.340 --> 00:11:14.040
Are you sure it's all right for me
to be wearing this?

00:11:14.110 --> 00:11:16.410
We've got no choice.

00:11:16.810 --> 00:11:18.580
It's all we have left here.

00:11:19.420 --> 00:11:21.650
The helmet connector is on the satchel.

00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:26.620
Yes. And now bring that to the front.
That's right.

00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:30.890
This way, I could help as an extra pilot.

00:11:31.130 --> 00:11:32.190
Don't be foolish.

00:11:32.260 --> 00:11:35.960
Just because you've got the outfit
doesn't mean you're ready for combat!

00:11:36.030 --> 00:11:37.260
But I...!

00:11:37.940 --> 00:11:41.230
It's okay. You remain here
or on the floor we were on earlier.

00:11:41.970 --> 00:11:42.870
Ensign Reccoa!

00:11:46.180 --> 00:11:46.970
Maybe that was thoughtless of me...!

00:11:52.820 --> 00:11:54.340
A red mobile suit!

00:11:54.420 --> 00:11:55.390
The Red Comet?!

00:11:55.720 --> 00:11:57.950
That isn't the Red Comet, is it?

00:11:59.060 --> 00:11:59.990
Watch out!

00:12:17.210 --> 00:12:18.200
Don't get in my way!

00:12:19.640 --> 00:12:21.270
Where is it?! Scan for the enemy!

00:12:23.510 --> 00:12:24.980
Hey! They reached our ship?!

00:12:28.690 --> 00:12:30.680
Commander, please wear your normal suit!

00:12:30.760 --> 00:12:32.810
I don't expect to be hit!
Why should I wear it?!

00:12:33.320 --> 00:12:35.990
Wear it! I'll take over
while you get changed!

00:12:36.060 --> 00:12:37.250
Give me a damage report!

00:12:37.760 --> 00:12:39.630
Is everything okay?

00:12:41.800 --> 00:12:43.730
These guys are accustomed
to real combat!

00:12:53.850 --> 00:12:55.110
Finally got one.

00:12:56.450 --> 00:12:57.240
Flares?

00:13:04.790 --> 00:13:07.020
Orders from the Bosnia to retreat?

00:13:07.930 --> 00:13:11.050
We've been lured away from our plan
because of that red mobile suit!

00:13:11.700 --> 00:13:14.360
Can't we win without the backup
from the mother ship?!

00:13:21.910 --> 00:13:23.460
We lost Eddy!

00:13:23.540 --> 00:13:24.570
I know!

00:13:24.640 --> 00:13:26.770
Did you think I didn't notice that
or something?!

00:13:26.840 --> 00:13:27.570
<i>No!</i>

00:13:27.650 --> 00:13:29.980
I hope our foe was the real Red Comet.

00:13:30.050 --> 00:13:31.480
Otherwise, this result is embarrassing.

00:13:38.260 --> 00:13:39.250
Awesome!

00:13:39.320 --> 00:13:41.190
Lieutenant Quattro shot down a mobile suit!

00:13:43.630 --> 00:13:45.220
Can't we proceed at full speed?

00:13:45.300 --> 00:13:47.590
At this rate, we could be hit
by a second wave.

00:13:47.670 --> 00:13:49.690
We shall count on Lieutenant Quattro.

00:13:49.770 --> 00:13:51.740
- Hurry with repairs to the engine.
- Yes, sir!

00:13:52.070 --> 00:13:54.470
Their retreat was awfully abrupt.

00:13:54.870 --> 00:13:56.170
What do you read from that, Captain?

00:13:56.610 --> 00:13:58.540
Bask came out and stopped us in our steps.

00:13:58.610 --> 00:14:01.580
So I imagine they'll be attacking
with a second wave.

00:14:10.190 --> 00:14:14.990
You are to open and read your orders when
the capsule following you becomes visible.

00:14:15.930 --> 00:14:16.890
Yes, sir!

00:14:16.960 --> 00:14:20.690
You have fifteen minutes to negotiate,
understood, Lieutenant Emma Sheen?

00:14:21.070 --> 00:14:21.960
Yes!

00:14:22.030 --> 00:14:24.590
Can we assume that capsule
is a powerful bomb of some sort?

00:14:25.440 --> 00:14:26.530
Something like that.

00:14:27.270 --> 00:14:30.470
Okay. I understand some of you are
piloting Hizacks for the first time...

00:14:30.540 --> 00:14:32.270
...but think of this
as some advanced training.

00:14:32.340 --> 00:14:36.250
The objective of this mission is to
negotiate the return of our Mk. IIs.

00:14:36.310 --> 00:14:40.310
Keep in mind that we'll be having
someone else lead this unit tomorrow!

00:14:46.120 --> 00:14:47.110
The A.E.U.G....!

00:14:53.430 --> 00:14:55.230
Hand-written orders, huh...

00:14:58.340 --> 00:15:00.400
I've located what appears
to be an enemy mobile suit!

00:15:00.600 --> 00:15:03.040
They're here! Is the Rick Dias
ready to go?

00:15:03.110 --> 00:15:04.630
- We're done!
- That's quick.

00:15:05.180 --> 00:15:07.510
They're approaching us
from a different angle this time!

00:15:07.580 --> 00:15:09.010
They're a separate mobile unit!

00:15:13.150 --> 00:15:14.520
Signal confirmed!

00:15:14.820 --> 00:15:16.620
- What?!
- Are you serious?!

00:15:16.890 --> 00:15:17.790
Cease-fire?!

00:15:17.860 --> 00:15:20.380
Yes! I'm told a white flag was confirmed!

00:15:21.330 --> 00:15:23.190
A mobile suit carrying a white flag?

00:15:23.260 --> 00:15:24.190
That's right!

00:15:33.040 --> 00:15:34.060
What do you think?

00:15:34.140 --> 00:15:37.010
We need to buy some time.

00:15:37.070 --> 00:15:38.340
We'll accept.

00:15:38.410 --> 00:15:41.240
At least until the Argama's main engine
is repaired.

00:15:56.430 --> 00:15:58.520
Arriving alone? That's very brave.

00:16:02.330 --> 00:16:04.490
I've brought a hand-written letter
from Captain Bask with me.

00:16:05.700 --> 00:16:09.660
If anyone approaches this mobile suit,
that Hizack will attack.

00:16:10.040 --> 00:16:12.510
- I hear she boarded alone.
- With a mobile suit?

00:16:12.580 --> 00:16:15.910
- With a Gundam! Unit One!
- She's pretty good looking.

00:16:15.980 --> 00:16:19.010
- Don't forget, she's a diehard Titan!
- You mean she's a fanatic?

00:16:33.760 --> 00:16:35.730
That's Lieutenant Emma Sheen, I recall.

00:16:36.430 --> 00:16:40.460
We wish for an immediate response
to Captain Bask Om's hand-written letter.

00:16:40.540 --> 00:16:41.630
That's a tough request.

00:16:48.380 --> 00:16:50.280
How shameless!

00:16:51.550 --> 00:16:54.210
Lieutenant, are you aware
of the contents of this letter?

00:16:54.290 --> 00:16:55.150
No.

00:16:55.220 --> 00:16:57.520
No wonder you can remain so calm.

00:17:09.430 --> 00:17:14.030
If you don't return Kamille Bidan
and the Gundam Mk. II to us...

00:17:14.270 --> 00:17:16.970
...Kamille's parents will be killed.

00:17:17.840 --> 00:17:19.310
Another Titan dirty tactic!

00:17:19.780 --> 00:17:21.240
I-I don't believe it!

00:17:22.050 --> 00:17:23.240
They're like the mafia!

00:17:23.310 --> 00:17:25.710
It's not something you'd expect from the
leader of a proper military unit!

00:17:25.780 --> 00:17:28.950
I-I can't believe Captain Bask
would do such thing.

00:17:29.020 --> 00:17:30.650
This was written by Bask himself!

00:17:30.720 --> 00:17:32.350
The contents are just
as you read, Lieutenant.

00:17:32.420 --> 00:17:35.590
I know. But this isn't something
the military would do.

00:17:35.830 --> 00:17:38.160
You're right! The Titans are not the military!

00:17:38.230 --> 00:17:39.290
They're mercenaries!

00:17:39.360 --> 00:17:41.060
A private army!

00:17:41.400 --> 00:17:44.460
However, they're still part of
the Earth Federation Forces!

00:17:47.340 --> 00:17:51.300
I, myself, have not agreed
to be part of Bask's private forces.

00:17:51.640 --> 00:17:53.270
Bask isn't at the top of this, Lieutenant!

00:17:53.540 --> 00:17:55.140
It's much larger than that.

00:17:55.210 --> 00:17:58.700
These are personal soldiers of people whose
spirits have been pulled by Earth's gravity!

00:17:59.020 --> 00:18:01.310
Not even Zeon would've thought up
something so pathetic.

00:18:01.390 --> 00:18:03.480
But this might be nothing but a bluff.

00:18:03.690 --> 00:18:05.120
Bask would do it.

00:18:05.620 --> 00:18:08.350
I know what he's capable of doing
more than anyone.

00:18:08.630 --> 00:18:09.620
Damn!

00:18:10.360 --> 00:18:12.090
<i>I heard they have hostages!</i>

00:18:12.160 --> 00:18:13.960
He amazes me, damn Bask!

00:18:14.600 --> 00:18:15.530
Did you hear?

00:18:15.600 --> 00:18:17.590
But how'd they ever get hostages?

00:18:17.670 --> 00:18:19.900
Because they're the parents
of that kid, Kamille.

00:18:21.740 --> 00:18:23.900
The hostages in exchange for the Mk. IIs?!

00:18:23.970 --> 00:18:26.270
- Bring up the Mk. IIs!
- Hostages?

00:18:26.740 --> 00:18:28.140
We still don't know
what'll become of this!

00:18:28.910 --> 00:18:30.140
Hey, did you know?!

00:18:30.210 --> 00:18:32.810
The kid's parents have been taken hostage!

00:18:32.880 --> 00:18:34.110
What kid?!

00:18:34.190 --> 00:18:36.150
What are you doing in a pilot suit?!

00:18:36.220 --> 00:18:38.420
Is it true?! What you just said?!

00:18:41.460 --> 00:18:44.890
Destroy the Hizacks close to the Argama,
and then we'll proceed!

00:18:45.960 --> 00:18:47.160
That would be highly risky.

00:18:47.730 --> 00:18:50.060
Do you suggest we do as Bask wishes?!

00:18:50.130 --> 00:18:51.860
<i>Unidentified capsule located!</i>

00:18:51.940 --> 00:18:53.340
- Capsule?!
- What is it?!

00:18:54.370 --> 00:18:56.310
- Send over an image of it!
- <i>Yes, sir!</i>

00:19:04.980 --> 00:19:06.950
That must be the capsule.

00:19:07.550 --> 00:19:09.490
- Send out the observation camera!
- <i>Yes, sir!</i>

00:19:17.600 --> 00:19:21.660
"If there are any signs of the enemy
trying to take the capsule, destroy it"!

00:19:22.830 --> 00:19:25.430
Is it a bomb powerful enough
to destroy the battleship?

00:19:26.340 --> 00:19:28.070
Roger that, Mr. Jamaican!

00:19:31.410 --> 00:19:32.500
Look inside that capsule...!

00:19:32.840 --> 00:19:34.400
Is there someone in it?!

00:19:36.580 --> 00:19:38.380
I'm sure you've realized now,
Lieutenant Emma!

00:19:38.450 --> 00:19:41.480
But there's only one person in there.
I don't see the other hostage!

00:19:41.550 --> 00:19:42.420
This can't be true!

00:19:42.490 --> 00:19:45.110
That must be a hologram!
It's nothing but an image.

00:19:45.190 --> 00:19:47.250
Bask isn't into such tricks!

00:19:47.590 --> 00:19:49.060
Is Kamille Bidan there?!

00:19:49.130 --> 00:19:51.490
Have him identify the person in the capsule!

00:19:51.560 --> 00:19:52.820
But Captain...!

00:20:00.670 --> 00:20:03.200
I'm not about to hand over something
we went through the trouble to get!

00:20:03.270 --> 00:20:04.470
No way!

00:20:08.850 --> 00:20:10.710
Gundam Mk. II, Unit 3, taking off!

00:20:13.350 --> 00:20:16.410
Don't get in my way!
I'm going to rescue my mom!

00:20:16.790 --> 00:20:18.410
I agree with Lieutenant Quattro!

00:20:18.490 --> 00:20:19.890
We're better off doing as Captain Bask...!

00:20:19.960 --> 00:20:20.950
We can't do that!

00:20:21.160 --> 00:20:23.460
Mk. II Unit 3 is taking off?!

00:20:23.530 --> 00:20:25.360
It's Kamille piloting it? But why?!

00:20:25.430 --> 00:20:26.860
- That guy?!
- That kid?

00:20:26.930 --> 00:20:27.950
Stop him!

00:20:28.030 --> 00:20:30.900
I think he knows who's
in the capsule.

00:20:35.410 --> 00:20:37.400
What is my mother doing out there?!

00:20:43.550 --> 00:20:44.950
Emma returned.

00:20:45.020 --> 00:20:47.450
But there should be a return signal.

00:20:49.390 --> 00:20:50.850
That's not her?!

00:20:52.320 --> 00:20:53.980
Emma should be in Unit 1!

00:20:57.290 --> 00:20:58.760
Is that unit trying to capture the capsule?!

00:21:20.750 --> 00:21:23.190
<i>This is always the case... always!</i>

00:21:23.250 --> 00:21:25.080
<i>You're always doing this to me.</i>

00:21:25.160 --> 00:21:27.680
What are you doing, way out here?!

00:21:33.030 --> 00:21:36.000
I hope you disintegrate
along with the bomb, Unit 3!

00:21:57.090 --> 00:21:59.580
What?! Nothing happened?

00:22:01.290 --> 00:22:02.690
Why didn't anything happen?

00:22:04.900 --> 00:22:07.960
And there's no damage to
the Mk. II's armor?

00:22:11.240 --> 00:22:11.930
What just happened here?

00:22:12.000 --> 00:22:14.560
What's this feeling of uneasiness?

00:22:47.270 --> 00:22:49.600
Oh, I can't help believing you

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
kanarazu aeru to ano hi kara shinjiteita

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
I've believed we're sure to meet again ever since that day

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
kitto yobiau kokoro ga areba

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
If we have heart, we'll be called together again

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
mugen no Energy yobisamasu

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
Awaken the infinite energy

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
aa kizutsukeau mae ni

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
Before you get hurt

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
dekiru koto sagashite Please

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
Find what you can do...Please

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
nagedasanai de kurushii toki koso

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
Don't throw it away because of this painful age

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
itsuka mita aoi sora wo

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
Until the day we gaze up again

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
kitto anata to miageru hi made

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
at the blue sky we once saw

00:23:48.770 --> 00:23:51.100
Upon her return to the Alexandria...

00:23:51.170 --> 00:23:54.700
...Emma Sheen expresses her disapproval
for the Titans' tactics led by Bask Om.

00:23:54.780 --> 00:23:57.750
This marks the beginning
of Emma's reawakening.

00:23:58.750 --> 00:24:02.620
Is Emma to become Kamille's new lover?

00:24:03.450 --> 00:24:07.410
Next on Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam,
"Emma's Decision."

00:24:07.470 --> 00:24:12.470
Next Episode

00:24:07.470 --> 00:24:12.470
Emma's Decision

00:24:08.160 --> 00:24:10.790
You will see the tears of time.
